parts.text:
R2 red, as expected: implementation returns insertion order (`atv_00000001` first), test expects sorted. Now implement sorting: order by first-encontro start, tie by título. Modify the GET /atividades handler to sort lines.

Sorting: get each linha's first encontro start. Compute inline.

```js
app.get('/atividades', exigirUsuario, (req, res) => {
  const linhas = banco.prepare(...).all();
  const ordenadas = linhas.map(linha => {
    const primeiros = encontrosPorAtividade.all(linha.id);
    return { linha, inicio: primeiros.length ? Date.parse(primeiros[0].inicio) : Infinity };
  }).sort((a, b) => a.inicio - b.inicio || a.linha.titulo.localeCompare(b.linha.titulo));
  res.json(ordenadas.map(x => serializarAtividade(x.linha)));
});
```

Tie-break by title using localeCompare? For "Zeta" vs "Bravo" — localeCompare gives correct ordering. In PT locale the comparison could differ (accents), but our data is ASCII. Use `localeCompare('pt-BR')`? Keep simple `localeCompare` default. Actually to be deterministic use `.localeCompare(b)` without locale.

Note: R2 says every activity has a 1º encontro (R8), so Infinity path never happens; but fallback harmless.

Implement.

